In his six years of his tenure, the Special Rapporteur was able to carry out 12 country visits (see below), all of which gave rise to a detailed mission report containing a description of the court system and the situation of the judges, prosecutors and lawyers as observed in the country, followed by specific recommendations:
• 2004: Kazakhstan, Brazil;
• 2005: Ecuador (twice), Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan;
• 2007: Maldives, Democratic Republic of the Congo;
• 2008: Russian Federation;
• 2009: Guatemala (three times).
